# Agent workflow — commits and testing

## Git: user commits everything

- **Never** run `git commit`, `git push`, `git add` (for the purpose of committing), or create/amend commits unless the user **explicitly** asks in that message (e.g. "commit this", "create a commit").
- "Implement the plan", "fix this", or "apply the changes" does **not** mean commit.
- After making changes, leave them **uncommitted** and tell the user what to review.
- If the user asks for a commit message suggestion, provide text only — do not run `git commit` unless they ask you to.
- Do not push to remote unless explicitly asked.

## Commit message format

When the user asks for a commit message, suggest **one concise line** using [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/):

```
<type>: <short description in imperative mood>
```

**Types:** `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `test`, `chore`, `build`, `ci`, `perf`, `a11y`

**Rules:**
- Lowercase type prefix, no scope unless it adds clarity (e.g. `fix(a11y): …`)
- Imperative mood: "add labels" not "added labels"
- One line, ~72 characters max — no body unless the user asks
- Describe **why/what**, not a file list

**Examples:**

```
feat: add skip link and main landmark
fix: meet AA contrast on muted text
fix(a11y): add visible labels to contact form
docs: add WCAG audit report
chore: update resume link
```

Provide the message ready to copy-paste; do not run `git commit`.

## Test before handoff

After each logical change (or phase of work), **run tests yourself** and report results before asking the user to commit.

For this project, use as appropriate:

| Check | Command |
|-------|---------|
| Build | `npm run build` |
| Local preview | `npm start` (http://localhost:3000) |
| Accessibility | `npx @axe-core/cli http://localhost:3000 --tags wcag2a,wcag2aa,wcag21aa,wcag22aa` |

- If a check fails, fix it or report the failure clearly — do not tell the user to commit broken work.
- Summarize what was tested and what the user should manually verify in the browser (layout, keyboard nav, etc.).

## Handoff format

When work is ready for the user to commit:

1. List changed files
2. Test results (pass/fail)
3. Suggested commit message(s) in conventional format (see above) — user copies and commits
4. Reminder that commits are theirs to make
